ves the new Pass-2 binary with no verify-eval case, so a mis-emission of forbids_contract_allowed_state is not caught by the eval gate"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In Scope/Testing, replace 'code-review eval corpus' with the explicit files: add the fire + two pass cases to code-review-tests.eval.yaml, and add (or explicitly decline, with rationale) a code-review-verify.eval.yaml case for forbids_contract_allowed_state.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Correct the ADR reference: name ADR 0082 (the two-lane impact decision ADR, formerly 0035) as the ADR the v4 lane-split supersedes/amends, and clarify whether ADR 0036 is bumped only for the version-cadence/cohort-reset aspect.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"indeterminate","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Pass-3 impact model code-v4 (`impact_code` in decide.py; ADR 0036 version bump)'","docs/adr/0036-...md:1 title 'Impact-model permissive rollout + version-segmented calibration cadence' — governs versioning cadence, not the lane shape","docs/adr/0082-code-review-two-lane-tier-tagged-impact.md:1 '# ADR 0082 — Code-review impact is a two-lane, tier-tagged, severity-first MAX' (renumbered from 0035) — this is the ADR whose lane/tier/floor decision v4 supersedes","decide.py comment attributes the model to 'story albite-lazy-barb', matching ADR 0082"],"finding":"The plan attributes the code-v4 lane-split redesign to 'ADR 0036 version bump', but ADR 0036 is the impact-model rollout/calibration-cadence ADR; the ADR that DEFINES impact_code's two-lane tier structure (the thing v4 changes) is ADR 0082 (renumbered from 0035), which the plan never names in Scope or Approach.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f66c7fadc7f1df8b7","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 ('Pass-3 impact model code-v4 ... ADR 0036 version bump') and Scope","norm_id":"n504c932937f3dc2e","pri